<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phrygians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Phrygians were an Indo-European people who settled in central and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> around 1200 BCE, probably migrating from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. They built a kingdom centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordion">Gordion</a> that flourished in the 8th century BCE under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midas">Midas</a>, wrote their language in an alphabet related to the Greek, and worshipped the mother goddess Matar. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phrygia">Phrygia</a> later fell under Lydian, Persian and Hellenistic rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phrygians.jpg" alt="Phrygians" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phrygians.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
